00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.950 align:start position:0%
it's a historic election in more ways  than one  it's the first time chileans will have a  say in who will write a new constitution  a document that will determine the  country's economic political  and social roadmap  gloria perez and her husband believe  it's no small feat  this will define our future that's why  this day is so special  in order to make the necessary changes  the social changes  that we've been waiting for for so long  chileans are also electing mayors  governors and city council members  but the constitutional vote is regarded  as the most significant  the current constitution written 40  years ago under the augusto pinochet  dictatorship  is regarded by a great many as  illegitimate  and the source of many of chile's ills  for the first time anywhere in the world  50  of delegates to a constitutional  convention will be women  17 of the 155 delegates will also  represent chile's indigenous people  their existence isn't even recognized in  the current constitution  and another first to prevent long lines  because of the pandemic  the election is taking place over two  rather than one day  that means these votes won't be counted  until sunday the end of the second day  in the meantime these bins will be taped  completely and  covered with seals that according to  electoral authorities  will break if anybody tries to tamper  with the votes  and then they will be taken to a special  security area and kept under guard by  the army  even so a lot of people don't trust the  system  that's why daniel who works in front of  his designated polling station  is staying out for nowhere  i can't wait to vote but tomorrow all of  us will go tomorrow because we've seen  in many countries that when they leave  the votes overnight  someone changes them while chile doesn't  have a reputation for vote tampering  it's a reflection of how discredited  political institutions  and politicians have become in this  country  where millions are waiting for a new  constitution to prioritize the social  rights of the majority  rather than the privileges of a minority  lucian newman al jazeera santiago
 

